# Reapply the input-remapper preset when the drawing tablet reconnects.
#
# The Intuos BT sleeps after a few minutes idle and must re-initiate the
# Bluetooth link itself (the host gets br-connection-create-socket if it tries),
# so every wake is a fresh device add. input-remapper's own autoload usually
# catches it, but not always - and it silently does nothing if the preset has
# been emptied. tablet-remap repairs the preset and restarts injection.
#
# Match the PAD only, so this fires once per connect rather than per node, and
# exclude input-remapper's own forwarded device - it carries the same name and
# would retrigger this rule in a loop. It is told apart by phys:
#   real       phys=f8:3d:c6:07:5f:2b        uniq=dc:2c:26:dc:c2:7e
#   forwarded  phys=input-remapper/f8:3d...  uniq=""
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", \
  ATTRS{name}=="Wacom* Pad", ATTRS{phys}!="input-remapper*", \
  TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="tablet-remap.service"
